From 3b7a4357186783774e72bcf0a463cc5f972bab57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:02:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 159/197] Unified: Fix design check and AI chat bugs found in
 review

Design check:
- Parts inside a hidden App::Part or group are skipped; placements are
  taken globally (Links no longer crash the check).
- Open shells and non-solid shapes are reported; only bodies are
  checked for split solids; tiny gaps below the tolerance do not count
  as floating.
- The pair cache key includes the edges, a vertex hash and the
  tolerances, so a moved hole is detected again.
- Parts whose placement is bound by an expression are not moved by
  the fix; the other part is moved instead.
- The background worker cleans up if it fails to start and does not
  open a console window on Windows.
- Closing the panel while "Fix all" runs cancels instead of raising,
  and the undo transaction is always closed.

AI chat:
- The bridge talks UTF-8 on all platforms (Windows pipes default to
  the ANSI code page).
- When FreeCAD goes away, pending tool calls are failed and the
  running turn is interrupted, so the bridge exits.
- "New conversation" interrupts the running turn and ignores its
  leftovers.
- run_python copes with code that closes the active document.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
